# Input graph written at repair (2026-10-30) for
# CatholicOS__ontokit-api__ontokit_services_ontology_extractor.py__OntologyMetadataExtractor__extract_description.
# Two owl:Ontology subjects, in this order in the file (the in-memory store
# yields them in insertion order): ex:OntoBare has no description, the
# blank node after it has only rdfs:comment. With ontology_iri=None the
# global loop must go past its first subject, and past the first two
# properties of the priority list, to answer — and it interpolates a BNode
# in subject position.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

ex:OntoBare a owl:Ontology .

[] a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:comment "Anonymous ontology, comment only." .
